cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SENTINEL in research, please cite the repository and the exact commit used."
title: "SENTINEL: Adaptive Cyber Deception Research Lab"
type: software
abstract: >-
  An open-source research framework for studying adaptive cyber deception inside bounded synthetic environments. SENTINEL combines matched multi-policy experiments, paired statistical reporting, explicit resource ceilings, versioned telemetry, and a local-first research laboratory. Current evidence is synthetic; the Adaptive policy is a deterministic heuristic.
keywords:
  - cyber deception
  - adaptive cyber deception
  - deception technology
  - synthetic decoy environments
  - reproducible research
  - cybersecurity experimentation
  - statistical evaluation
authors:
  - family-names: Zopair
    given-names: SENTINEL contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/zopair/SENTINEL"
url: "https://zopair.github.io/SENTINEL/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
